{"decision":"promote","rationale":"I found no demonstrated contract violation. The mechanical integrity checks are clean in all 28 cases: address_mismatch_pairs is 0 and model admissions_without_recorded_latency is 0. Oracle-side unpaired admissions are identical to the incumbent's, and matched-read counts move by at most about 200 reads per case, so neither coverage nor cancellation explains the comparison. The candidate changes the incumbent in two ways, and both are declared, bounded parameters. First, pre_wait=1 (range 0–4): a precharge that waits on the bank's tRAS or tRTP limit issues one cycle after that limit. This does not apply when write recovery sets the limit, which the model tracks with a new per-bank pre_after_write flag. Second, pending_unforced=1 (range 0–1): the expected writebacks of reads already in flight also lengthen a write mode that began because the read queue was empty. Both objectives improve on both groups. Core error falls on training (0.0965% to 0.0860%, −0.0105 pp, −10.9%) and on validation (0.4579% to 0.4460%, −0.0119 pp, −2.6%). MAE/L falls on training (0.08484 to 0.08469, −0.18%) and on validation (0.05712 to 0.05521, −3.3%). The worst individual cores improve: val7 goes from −5.052% to −4.848% (−0.204 pp, −4.0%) and lbm from 0.431% to 0.295% (−0.136 pp, −31.5%). Validation tails also improve: P99.9/L −1.3%, the tail metric −1.8%, reads above 5L −2.9% and reads above 1L −1.2%. The improvements are broad. For core error, 8 of 14 training cases and 9 of 14 validation cases improve, and summed gains exceed summed regressions by about 9 times on training and 3 times on validation. For MAE/L, 10 of 14 training cases and 12 of 14 validation cases improve. The costs are real but smaller. val2 core error is about 2.9 times larger (+0.044 pp) and val5 rises 17% (+0.040 pp), both toward overprediction. Validation core error without val7 is +2.7%. Training reads above 5L rise by 59 (+1.4%), and absolute drift/L rises on both groups. The candidate also improves on the rejected iteration-9 pre_wait variant, which worsened core error on both groups. It keeps its roughly 99% core-error and 84–90% MAE/L reduction relative to the stage-entry FixedLat baseline.","improvements":["Training mean core error: 0.096505% → 0.086019% (−0.0105 pp, −10.9%). Largest driver is lbm, the worst training case: 0.4308% → 0.2951% (−0.136 pp, −31.5%). Also better: arizona −0.011 pp, bravo −0.009 pp, llama7b 0.0086% → 0.0008%. 8 of 14 cases improve and 5 regress; summed gains are about 0.165 pp against about 0.018 pp of regressions.","Validation mean core error: 0.457919% → 0.445976% (−0.0119 pp, −2.6%). The dominant failure, val7, improves from −5.052% to −4.848% (−0.204 pp, −4.0%), with its reads above 5L 439 → 422. Also better: val1 −0.016 pp, val8 −0.017 pp, val14 −0.006 pp. 9 of 14 cases improve and 4 regress; summed gains are about 0.252 pp against about 0.084 pp of regressions.","Validation MAE/L: 0.057115 → 0.055205 (−3.3%); still −1.6% without val5. 12 of 14 cases improve, including val5 −11.4%, val12 −22.9%, val13 −43.5%, val8 −3.6%, val14 −3.6% and val1 −2.5%. The only regression is val11 at +0.17%.","Training MAE/L: 0.084841 → 0.084686 (−0.18%), with 10 of 14 cases better, including llama7b −54%, maxclique −7.9%, omnetpp −1.5% and lbm −0.34%.","Validation tails: P99.9/L 2.393 → 2.361 (−1.3%); tail metric 0.757 → 0.743 (−1.8%); reads above 5L 1,743 → 1,692 (−51, −2.9%); reads above 1L 80,622 → 79,636 (−1.2%). Per case: val14 reads above 5L 531 → 489; val1 P99.9/L −6.8%; val5 reads above 1L −14.6%.","Training reads above 1L: 221,220 → 220,258 (−0.43%; −0.45% without lbm). lbm reads above 5L 56 → 50 and its extreme errors shrink (+1,335/−1,955 → +1,234/−1,826 cycles).","Signed core-error bias shrinks in magnitude on both groups: training +0.067% → +0.059%, validation −0.398% → −0.377%.","Coverage and integrity are unchanged: identical oracle-side unpaired admissions, negligible changes in matched reads, and zero address mismatches and zero admissions without recorded latency in all 28 cases.","Compared with stage-entry FixedLat: training core error 23.67% → 0.086% (−99.6%) and validation 24.90% → 0.446% (−98.2%). MAE/L falls 84.4% on training and 89.6% on validation. Reads above 5L: 6,445 → 4,140 on training and 3,100 → 1,692 on validation."],"accepted_regressions":["val2 core error 0.0236% → 0.0677% (+0.044 pp, about 2.9 times larger, overprediction). Its largest overprediction grows from 754 to 1,108 cycles and its reads above 5L from 13 to 16, although its MAE/L improves 7.4% and reads above 1L fall by 31.","val5 core error 0.234% → 0.274% (+0.040 pp, +17%, overprediction), although its MAE/L improves 11.4% and its tails shrink.","Validation mean core error without val7: 0.1045% → 0.1073% (+0.0028 pp, +2.7%). Outside the dominant failure the validation core-error gain is not present.","Training tails: reads above 5L 4,081 → 4,140 (+59, +1.4%); P99.9/L 3.160 → 3.166 (+0.19%); tail metric +0.7%. arizona contributes most (reads above 5L 450 → 493, MAE/L +1.5%, P99.9/L +0.8%).","Mean absolute drift/L rises on both groups: training +2.3%, validation +4.9%. Per-case drift moves further toward overprediction on val2, val5 and val7 (val7 +0.0205 → +0.0231, largest overprediction 483 → 565 cycles).","Small training core-error regressions: whisper +0.0084 pp, whiskey +0.0039 pp (MAE/L +0.36%, tail metric +2.8%), gap_bfs +0.0034 pp and gap_sssp +0.0019 pp.","val11: tail metric +4.4%, P99 91 → 95 cycles, P99.9/L +0.6%, while its core error improves slightly."],"contract_findings":["The diff against the incumbent has two parts. (1) pre_wait, declared through p.number with range 0–4, default 0, set to 1: it is added to the precharge slot unless write recovery set the bank's precharge limit. Write recovery is tracked by a new pre_after_write flag, updated in finish_column and slip_after and reset in open_row; finish_column now assigns the limit conditionally instead of taking a max, which is otherwise equivalent. (2) pending_unforced, declared with range 0–1, set to 1: pending_writebacks now also covers write mode entered because the read queue emptied, counting from drain_start, and it applies at read admission only when the buffer is at or above the low watermark.","Each read's completion is computed once in predict() and returned; nothing revises an issued prediction. slip_after moves only the model's own calendar entries and bank limits, which is unchanged from the incumbent.","The inputs are hardware timings and watermarks, the current request's decoded levels, its address (used only to match a buffered write for forwarding, as in the incumbent), and statistics of the model's own past admissions and predictions (write_share EWMA, outstanding reads). I found no use of future requests, oracle completions or internals, workload names, specific addresses or evaluation identities.","No new command scheduler is added. The write-mode replay and its exit hysteresis already exist in the incumbent; pending_unforced only changes an expected count derived from past statistics. The model keeps growing more controller-like, but there is still no per-cycle command selection and no revision of issued predictions, so this is not a demonstrated violation.","Minor code issues, none a contract problem: precharge() does not clear pre_after_write, which is harmless because the bank is then marked precharged and its precharge limit is not consulted; Booking.inserted is set but unused, inherited from the incumbent; source comments say pre_wait was excluded after write recovery because of closed-loop core-cycle results, which is ordinary use of numerical training and validation feedback.","Mechanical integrity: address_mismatch_pairs is 0 and model admissions_without_recorded_latency is 0 in all 28 training and validation cases, and oracle-side unpaired admissions match the incumbent exactly."],"contract_violation":false,"uncertainty":["The gains are concentrated. lbm supplies nearly all of the training core-error gain (−1.2% without it), val7 all of the validation core-error gain (+2.7% without it), and val5 about 61% of the validation MAE/L gain. Outside these cases the change is roughly neutral on core error.","Each figure comes from a single closed-loop run. Changes of about 0.01 pp in core error or tens of reads in the 5L counts may be within the perturbation noise of closed-loop feedback.","The two mechanisms were evaluated only together, so their contributions are not separated. The val2 and val5 overprediction regressions and the higher drift could come from pending_unforced over-extending write mode in write-heavy phases, or from the one-cycle precharge delay.","val7 remains a −4.8% core-level underprediction and dominates the validation mean. The candidate reduces it but does not address its cause.","The write-recovery exclusion for pre_wait was chosen from closed-loop outcomes, after the unrestricted pre_wait candidate was rejected. That choice carries some tuning risk, although validation core error and MAE/L both improve.","Only single-core cases exist in this stage, so behavior under multicore contention with the new write-mode extension is not measured."]}
